# Project principles

Agentic Portfolio Lab is an auditable local paper-investing system. It is a
learning project, not financial advice or an oracle.

Authoritative contract: `AGENTS.md`. Details live in `docs/` (especially
`docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design-principles.md`, `docs/project-charter.md`,
`docs/roadmap.md`, `docs/backlog.md`, `docs/open-questions.md`, and
`docs/decisions/`). Do not duplicate or contradict those documents.

v0.1.0 is the known-good baseline. Do not expand scope just to make a test or
demo pass.

## Core rules

- AI proposes; deterministic code validates and owns financial state.
- Human approval is required before managed BUY execution.
- HOLD is a legitimate terminal decision and must never become executable.
- No synthetic fallback in durable/live mode (`AGENTIC_PORTFOLIO_LAB_DB_PATH`
  set). The unset-path in-memory demo API is not the paper-trading workflow.
- Missing evidence is explicit, never fabricated.
- Provider provenance and timestamps must remain truthful.
- Exact `SecurityIdentity` lineage matters; do not collapse identity to ticker.
- Immutable historical artifacts must not be rewritten.
- Managed and benchmark portfolios remain distinct.
- Financial calculations belong in domain/application code, not frontend JS.
- Frontend renders authoritative backend state and posts existing commands.
- SQLite is the current durable store. Do not commit the DB or provider keys.
- Do not touch `data/` or `ui-prototypes/` unless the user explicitly asks.

If a requested change conflicts with these rules, stop and surface the conflict.
